From 904f650004b8e335880b2b983f9c4d15dce186f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 10:52:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci): give the deploy-safety smoke tests the port the
 server listens on
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

master is still red after the type-check fix. Run #224 got as far as the
"Deploy-safety smoke tests" step and reported `0 passed, 12 failed`, every
one of them `fetch failed url=http://localhost:3001/...`.

Nothing is wrong with the assertions or the server. start-production.mjs
binds `PORT` and defaults to 3000; every URL in that step is 3001, and the
step never set PORT. The server came up healthy on 3000, the readiness loop
spent its full 60 x 2s expiring against 3001 (hence the step's 2m06s), and
then all twelve checks failed to connect. Reproduced locally: identical
failure without PORT, `12 passed, 0 failed` with `PORT=3001`.

The step is also changed to say which of the two things happened. A server
that never binds and a server that rejects everything produced byte-identical
output before — twelve "fetch failed" lines — which is exactly why this read
as a broken app rather than a missing variable. It now fails immediately with
an explicit message and dumps the supervisor log, and dumps it too when the
checks themselves fail.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QGy3NZWndBAVM8qKdAzXm1
---
 .github/workflows/ci.yml | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 12c3de0..0888f23 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -58,17 +58,33 @@ jobs:
       # Placeholders are enough because every check asserts a REJECTION.
       - name: Deploy-safety smoke tests
         run: |
-          node scripts/start-production.mjs &
+          node scripts/start-production.mjs > /tmp/start-production.log 2>&1 &
           SERVER_PID=$!
+          READY=0
           for i in $(seq 1 60); do
-            if curl -sf http://localhost:3001/health >/dev/null 2>&1; then break; fi
+            if curl -sf http://localhost:3001/health >/dev/null 2>&1; then READY=1; break; fi
             sleep 2
           done
+          # Without this branch a server that never binds looks exactly like a
+          # server that rejects every request: the loop just expires and all
+          # twelve checks report "fetch failed", which is what hid a missing
+          # PORT. Say which of the two happened, and show the server log.
+          if [ "$READY" -ne 1 ]; then
+            echo "::error::start-production.mjs never answered on http://localhost:3001/health"
+            cat /tmp/start-production.log
+            kill $SERVER_PID 2>/dev/null || true
+            exit 1
+          fi
           node scripts/verify-deploy-smoke.mjs http://localhost:3001
           STATUS=$?
+          if [ "$STATUS" -ne 0 ]; then cat /tmp/start-production.log; fi
           kill $SERVER_PID 2>/dev/null || true
           exit $STATUS
         env:
+          # start-production.mjs listens on PORT (default 3000); every URL in
+          # this step is 3001. Without this the server comes up healthy on the
+          # wrong port and all twelve checks fail with "fetch failed".
+          PORT: "3001"
           VITE_SUPABASE_URL: https://placeholder.supabase.co
           VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY: ci-placeholder
           NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL: https://placeholder.supabase.co
